{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310698,"nonce":"c6lZdmxbDqQ+/rmeyF4Y2MfiFxY=","title":"Adding scope-exit Free emission for @:shared classes (one-line change in compute_drop_behavior at hir_to_mir.rs:~1086) breaks the runtime ...","message":"**Status: OPEN. Operational half of [[bugs-pool-data-flow-gap]].**\n\n\nThe smoking gun at [hir_to_mir.rs:1100-1102](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L1100-L1102) is:\n\n```rust\nif self.is_stdlib_class_by_symbol(symbol) {\n    return DropBehavior::RuntimeManaged;  // ← no Free emitted\n}\n```\n\nExtern stdlib classes (Tensor, QTensor) return `RuntimeManaged`, so the compiler emits NO `rayzor_tensor_free` at scope-exit. That's why the tensor pool stayed dark (`hits=0 pushes=0`) even with @:shared landed in commit `c7e0ed7+2c76811+7638588`.\n\nThe one-line proposed fix:\n\n```rust\nif self.derive_shared_classes.contains(symbol_id) {\n    return DropBehavior::AutoDrop;  // @:shared → Free at scope-exit\n}\n// ... then EXTERN check below\n```\n\nBuild clean, 709 lib tests pass — BUT 1B llama-chat crashes EXIT=139 at `[gen] streaming` (previously worked).\n\n\nThe runtime free does atomic-decrement and only releases at refcount==1. So in principle, \"missed Free = leak, not UAF.\" But the bug is the opposite: **too many Frees on a single refcount**.\n\nWhen the user writes `var b = a`, the compiler currently:\n1. Reads the IrId of `a` (a `*mut RayzorTensor`)\n2. Binds `b` to that same IrId (no arc_clone emission)\n3. Both bindings reference the SAME atomic refcount = 1\n\nWhen `a` goes out of scope, the Free fires → refcount 1→0 → tensor released. `b` now points at freed memory. On next use → SIGSEGV.\n\n\nTwo complementary compiler emissions:\n\n1. **arc_clone on bind-from-shared-source**: every `var b = a` where `a` is a @:shared class binding becomes `var b = arc_clone(a)`. The atomic fetch_add publishes both bindings as ref-holders. Function-arg passing, struct field assignment, array push — all need the same treatment.\n   - Cost: ~5ns per assignment from a shared binding to a new binding (Relaxed fetch_add)\n   - Allocation count on a 24-token decode: a few thousand at most, so ~milliseconds budget — invisible\n\n2. **Free on scope-exit / reassign**: the one-line gate above. Decrement; release only at count==1.\n\nWe shipped (2) without (1). Doing only (2) is unsound — the FIRST scope-exit kills the tensor while siblings still hold it.\n\n\nIn `hir_to_mir.rs`, the Variable RHS lowering path. Specifically: when lowering `var b = a;` where `a`'s resolved class is in `derive_shared_classes` AND the assignment is NOT a final consume (the analyser must distinguish \"alias-clone\" from \"move-into-new-binding\"). Pattern is similar to the existing `derive_clone_classes` Tier B branch but fires implicitly on binding creation, not on explicit `.clone()`.\n\nAlso fires on:\n- Function call argument site (each call to `fn(x: Tensor)` passing a binding `t` needs `arc_clone(t)`)\n- Return value (`return tensor;` from a function that returns @:shared)\n- Struct/class field assignment from a binding\n- Array push from a binding\n- Closure capture from a binding (for closures called more than once)\n\nEach of these is a place where Haxe's GC-style semantics implicitly say \"new reference; both can be used.\" Under @:shared, we make that \"implicit Arc-clone.\"\n\n\nThe current arrangement (commits c7e0ed7+2c76811+7638588) is architecturally correct but operationally incomplete. The atoms, refcount field, view-pins-parent cascade, addInto debug-assert — all sound. Adding the missing arc_clone-on-bind compiler pass closes the loop without any runtime change.\n\nCost: substantial compiler refactor (~200-400 LOC across hir_to_mir's Variable RHS lowering + Call lowering + Return lowering + Field-assign lowering). But mechanical — same shape repeated at each binding-creation site.\n\n\n**Option B — stay with current state**: @:shared routes explicit `.clone()` to arc_clone, suppresses MarkMoved/CheckLive, but no auto-Free emission. Operational pool wiring stays dark. LlamaModel.hx:65 stays fixed (because explicit `.clone()` does bump the refcount). Architectural foundation is solid; pool just doesn't activate.\n\n**Option C — function-end Free only**: emit Free at function-end / return-with-value, but NOT at intermediate block-scope exits. Catches function-local temps (the common case for activation tensors) without the aliasing-rebind problem. Compromise that delivers partial pool wiring without the full arc-clone-on-bind machinery. Risk: some patterns might still alias dangerously; needs careful audit.\n\n\n- [[project-shared-arc-tensors]] — the architectural foundation this builds on\n- [[bugs-pool-data-flow-gap]] — the user-visible gap; this is its operational half\n- [[bugs-addinto-rebind-clone-drop-failure]] — already closed by current @:shared (explicit clone path)\n- [[project-move-clone-enforced]] — the @:move regime preserved for non-shared classes\n\n\nTried A.full: arc_clone-on-bind helper across Variable RHS + Call args + Return + Field-assign + Array push + enable Free gate. Reverted because the work was a **pure leak** — every tensor stayed alive forever, hiding the bugs. Three converged verifier findings (all file:line cited):\n\n\n`compute_drop_behavior` flipping to `AutoDrop` for `@:shared` was dead code because the upstream tracking uses `is_heap_alloc` gate at [hir_to_mir.rs:4791](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L4791), which is true ONLY for `HirExprKind::New`. Tensors come from `Tensor.zeros()` / `matmul()` / `fromBytesF32()` = `HirExprKind::Call`. They never enter `owned_heap_values`, so `IrInstruction::Free` is never emitted.\n\n**Fix for next attempt**: drop the `is_heap_alloc` gate for `@:shared` classes — register Tensor/QTensor Let bindings regardless of RHS shape (Call, Variable, Field all need tracking).\n\n\n[cranelift_backend.rs:3824-3841](compiler/src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs#L3824-L3841) calls `libc::free(ptr)` directly. Even if Free WERE emitted for a tensor, it would:\n- Skip the atomic `fetch_sub` (refcount stays \u003e 0)\n- Skip pool admission\n- Leak `data` / `shape` / `strides` allocations (only the wrapper struct is freed)\n- Create dangling pointers for every aliasing arc_clone handle\n\n**Fix for next attempt**: route `IrInstruction::Free` through `rayzor_{tensor,qtensor}_free` when the type is `@:shared`. The runtime free does the atomic decrement; only the count-to-zero thread runs the actual release.\n\n**These two defects cancel today** (tracking is broken so Free is never emitted, so the libc-free landmine is never stepped on), but landing arc_clone-on-bind alone would flip the cancellation and trigger immediate UAF.\n\n\n[hir_to_mir.rs:4826](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L4826) currently does `owned_heap_values.remove(\u0026src_sym)` when RHS is a Variable — transferring ownership from source binding to destination. For `@:shared`, BOTH bindings should keep independent refs after arc_clone. The remove drops the source's Free, leaving the source binding's lifetime untracked.\n\n**Fix for next attempt**: guard `owned_heap_values.remove(src_sym)` with `!derive_shared_classes.contains(\u0026src_class)` at Let (4826) AND Assign (5196, 5214) paths.\n\n\n[hir_to_mir.rs:5390](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L5390) excludes the returned symbol from scope cleanup, on the theory that the caller takes ownership. Under `@:shared`, the return-site arc_clone has ALREADY published a new ref for the caller; the function-local binding still needs its own Free.\n\n**Fix for next attempt**: swap `cleanup_all_scopes_except_symbol` → `cleanup_all_scopes` at line 5390 when the returned expression triggered Site 3 arc_clone.\n\n\n[lower_function_body at hir_to_mir.rs:3472-3476](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L3472-L3476) doesn't register `@:shared` parameters in `owned_heap_values`. Every Site 5 call-arg arc_clone leaks +1 ref per shared-class parameter per call.\n\n**Fix for next attempt**: register `@:shared` params via owned_heap_values during lower_function_body.\n\n\n[hir_to_mir.rs:5204](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L5204) doesn't include shared-class Variable RHS. The arc_cloned destination is never registered for scope-exit Free.\n\n**Fix for next attempt**: `|| shared_class_for_alias_clone(rhs).is_some()` in `rhs_needs_tracking`.\n\n\n- Site 8: for-in element bind at `lower_for_in_loop:30023` — `for (t in tensors)` doesn't arc_clone the loop variable\n- Site 9: switch-arm payload at `bind_pattern_with_scrutinee_type:24472-24572` — `case Some(t):` doesn't arc_clone\n\nLatent today (Free never fires) but UAF the moment defects 1+2 are fixed.\n\n\nRegression suite is insensitive to pure leaks. 1B + 8B both \"passed\" the work because every tensor stayed alive forever. Add a runtime test that asserts `RAYZOR_POOL_STATS pushes \u003e= 1` for a hot allocation path before re-landing.\n\n\n[quant.rs:2653](runtime/src/quant.rs#L2653) — only `QSCHEME_INT8` pool-routes. Llama-3.2-1B / 8B are Q4_K_M, so even with a working refcount the pool ceiling is F32 activations only. Lift this for at-rest pool admission.\n\n\nThe 11 fixes above must land **together as a single cohesive patch** — the verifier explicitly called out that landing arc_clone-on-bind alone is the UAF time-bomb. Order:\n\n1. Track shared-class bindings regardless of `is_heap_alloc` (defect 1)\n2. Route `IrInstruction::Free` → `rayzor_{tensor,qtensor}_free` (defect 2)\n3. Flip `cleanup_all_scopes_except_symbol → cleanup_all_scopes` for shared returns (defect 4)\n4. Guard `owned_heap_values.remove(src_sym)` (defect 3)\n5. Extend `rhs_needs_tracking` (defect 6)\n6. Register `@:shared` params (defect 5)\n7. Cover Sites 8 + 9 (defects 7+8)\n8. Runtime refcount-balance unit test (defect 9)\n9. Q4_K_M pool admission (defect 10)\n10. Re-introduce arc_clone-on-bind helper\n11. Re-introduce the AutoDrop gate\n\nEstimated scope: 400-600 LOC across `hir_to_mir.rs` + `cranelift_backend.rs` + `quant.rs` + a new unit test. Substantial, but mechanical given the file:line list above.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_shared_needs_arc_clone_on_bind` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}